    "did_you_know": "Photographs fired onto enamel do not fade and look as fresh today as the day they came out of the kiln.",
    "description": "The image celebrates the d’Orléans family, who abdicated the French throne during the Revolution of 1848 and settled in England. The setting for this group portrait is Orléans House in Twickenham, where the d’Orléans hosted numerous grand social events such as the garden party that occasioned this sitting.",
